==Old English==

===Etymology===
From Germanic ''*stōdh-'', from Indo-European ''*sta-, *stə-'' ‘stand, set’.  Cognate with Old High German ''[[stuot]]'' (German ''[[Stute]]'' ‘mare’), Old Norse ''stóð'' (Swedish ''[[sto]]'' ‘mare’). The Indo-European root is also the source of Old Slavic ''stado''<!--wrong script for Old Slavic-->

